adapters, including all objects, configuration readbacks and refresh coverage. Refresh now accepts the provider's aggregated task IDs while requiring every requested URL exactly once in the completed response; it preserves the existing polling bounds.\n\nThe TEST ONLY two-stage drill reuses public signed fixtures and retains bounded actual SDK exchanges, partial effects, network-guard counts and cleanup outcomes. Production activation remains disabled.\n\nValidation: tests-first SDK and input regressions; 49 SDK tests, 16 input tests, four repository contracts and the complete local suite passed (one existing local RPM-tool skip). The native→SDK drill passed all 20 scenarios before the final explicit socket-cleanup adjustment; its four cleanup regressions first failed and all 16 input tests then passed without ResourceWarning. Independent Standards and Spec review closed three evidence/guard/cleanup findings. Linux CI runs the final source and the existing native and four-client suites.\n\nOne earlier native preparation failed in the unchanged RPM verifier; its cause remains unknown. A separate same-bytes path probe proved an independent verifier defect, handled in a separate change.\n\nThis PR is based on merged RPM verifier repair #79; its six other reviewed file bytes are unchanged, and the Changelog retains both entries.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-22T17:53:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T17:53:38Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"0383c7818d51b8d819f95d7c0f81822abe478a56","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"No8blackball","id":17797708,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3Nzk3NzA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17797708?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/No8blackball","html_url":"https://github.com/No8blackball","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/No8blackball/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/No8bla